        "Emphasizes that human goals remain central to designing multi-agent workflows"
      ],
      "design_implication": "When product teams design software exclusively for human interaction, workflows frequently fail to accommodate downstream autonomous agents that execute tasks asynchronously. Mapping multi-stakeholder ecosystems now requires accounting for programmatic users alongside human operators. Start by mapping out agent touchpoints in complex service blueprints to identify where automated actors require structured status logs and explicit permission boundaries.",
